seg-b351230999a8 = Published CAI primary-paper numeric vectors (Cheinet { "2008" } transfer function; Peters/Freier sensitivity): k_eff·T² matched exactly, shot-noise ASD a one-sided floor within ~{ "2" }× of each published instrument (real devices carry technical noise above the quantum floor). A bracket, not parity. { "0.30" } round { "2" } (pre-registered fcb9ac64), a finding (stays MODELLED): the QPN-only rotation noise against the measured Gauguet et al. { "2009" } Fig. { "14" } points gives ratios { "0.695" } to { "0.788" } at the three admitted points ({ "0.751" } at the operating point), missing the pre-registered { "30" } % bar by { "0.5" } points; the QPN floor sits { "21" } to { "31" } % below the measured noise, as expected of a model without laser and detection noise. The gradiometer composition matches the Janvier et al. { "2022" } QPN model line (ratio { "1.013" } to { "1.017" }, Reference). The measured test cannot discriminate a sqrt({ "2" }) composition error; only the unequal-contrast Janvier line can <em>(ExternalDataset)</em>

